Subject: [DRAFT] AI COLUMN: add session variable ai_column_strict_read

NOT COMPILED, NOT RUN. src/share/system_variable/ob_system_variable_init.{h,cpp},
ob_sys_var_class_type.h and ob_system_variable_alias.h are generated from this
json by src/share/system_variable/gen_ob_sys_variables.py; regenerate (and check
whether src/share/system_variable/standalone_default_system_variable.extra needs
a matching entry) before building.

Requirements taken from the shipped tests (proven):

  * tools/deploy/mysql_test/test_suite/ai_column/t/ai_column_retry_strict.test:48
      select @@ai_column_strict_read as strict_read_defaults_off;
    .../r/mysql/ai_column_retry_strict.result:29-30  -> value must be **0**
    So the default is OFF; a non-default-on switch is mandatory or the DML and
    worker tests would fail on their first read.
  * same file lines 54,61,87,107,111,132,135: `SET SESSION
    ai_column_strict_read = ON|OFF` -> SESSION scope is what is exercised.
    A SESSION-only bool is a well-trodden shape in this file, e.g.
    "pseudo_slave_mode" (id 10292, data_type bool, flags "SESSION",
    default_value/base_value "0"), json lines 5076-5083.
  * The variable is checked at *execution* time (a statement on the same table
    errors before and after the task rows are cleaned -- test lines 68-86 vs
    107-110), so it must be reachable from the executor's session info, i.e.
    keep it a plain session var rather than a tenant config.

The id is the next free one after the current maximum (10753 =
ob_sparse_drop_ratio_search, json lines 10964-10978). Confirm the generator does
not require ids to be allocated from a reserved range before accepting 10754.

